CONTEXT: There is a bug in `objToLocalTS` in /luxon/src/impl/util.js. The function currently is:

export function objToLocalTS(obj) {
  let d = Date.UTC(
    obj.year,
    obj.month - 1,
    obj.day,
    obj.hour,
    obj.minute,
    obj.second,
    obj.millisecond
  );

  // for legacy reasons, years between 0 and 99 are interpreted as 19XX; revert that
  if (obj.year < 100 && obj.year >= 0) {
    d = new Date(d);
    d.setUTCFullYear(d.getUTCFullYear() - 1900);
  }
  return +d;
}

The bug: for years 0..99, the day-of-month overflow is normalized in the 19XX/20XX calendar first and only then is the year changed. Because year 2000 is a leap year but year 100 is not (and year 1900 is not a leap year but year 0 is), dates that overflow into January/February of the next year come out wrong. Example: DateTime.fromISO("0099-12-31").plus({ days: 61 }) currently yields 0100-03-01 but must yield 0100-03-02 (Dec 31 of year 99 + 61 days = Mar 2 of year 100, because February of year 100 has 28 days).

TASK:
