2) Apply exactly this change to the `if (obj.year < 100 && obj.year >= 0)` branch (keep the comment lines):

  if (obj.year < 100 && obj.year >= 0) {
    d = new Date(d);
    // set the month and day again, this is necessary because year 2000 is a leap year, but year 100 is not
    d.setUTCFullYear(obj.year, obj.month - 1, obj.day);
  }

  Change nothing else in the file.
3) VERIFY with a scratch script run via `cd /luxon && npx babel-node /tmp/check2.js` (babel-node is a devDependency; if it fails, use `npx jest` with a temporary test file placed in /tmp and a custom --rootDir, or @babel/register). The script must import { DateTime } from "/luxon/src/luxon.js" and print, using UTC zone ({ zone: "utc" } where needed):
