CONTEXT: /luxon/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js defines a zone with a fixed offset. Its constructor is currently:

  constructor(offset) {
    super();
    /** @private **/
    this.fixed = offset;
  }

and its `get isValid()` unconditionally returns `true`. That is wrong: constructing a FixedOffsetZone with a non-numeric offset (e.g. `new FixedOffsetZone("blorp")` or `new FixedOffsetZone(NaN)`) produces a zone that claims to be valid but has a NaN offset, so a DateTime built on it is silently corrupt instead of invalid. The class must report itself invalid in that case, and the invalid zone must not produce a bogus name. The sibling class /luxon/src/zones/invalidZone.js is the model: it has `get isValid() { return false; }`.

